# 1-based lines to bookmark, one per line. Blank lines and # comments ignored.
#
# JSON has no declarations: the structure a reader navigates by is the key
# path. `pair` is the only kind with a name (its `key`), so it is the single
# landmark and container, and each line below should anchor on the keys above
# it and show them as breadcrumbs.

# `customer.name` — one level down. Ends in a separator comma, which must not
# widen the target to the enclosing object.
6

# `customer.address.city` — two levels down, so the breadcrumb walk has to
# name both enclosing pairs.
10

# `customer.address.country` — the last member, with no trailing comma.
11

# `lines[1].discount` — inside an object inside an array. The object and array
# are anonymous, so the breadcrumb names `lines` and nothing between.
28

# `totals.tax.rate` — two levels down in a different branch, so a query that
# lost a key would also match nothing here or something under `customer`.
34

# `tags` — a pair whose value is an array, directly under the root object.
39

# NOT bookmarkable, kept here as a record rather than silently omitted:
#
#   17    "description": "Widget, large",
#   26    "unit_price": 80,
#
# Every key here also appears in the sibling element of `lines`, and objects in
# an array are anonymous — nothing in the path tells element 0 from element 1,
# so codemark refuses the query as ambiguous. The same identical-siblings
# limitation as Scala's; line 28 works only because `discount` is unique to its
# element.
